{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"mcr.microsoft.com/azurelinux/base/nginx","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:12:07.869Z","source":{"name":"Microsoft Artifact Registry","api":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/api/v1/catalog/azurelinux/base/nginx/details?reg=mar","page":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/en-us/product/azurelinux/base/nginx/about"},"readme":"## About\n\nThis repository contains the official Nginx image for Azure Linux.\n\n### What is Azure Linux?\n\nAzure Linux is a Linux distribution for Microsoft’s cloud infrastructure and edge products and services. Azure Linux is designed to provide a consistent platform for these devices and services and will enhance Microsoft’s ability to stay current on Linux updates.  \n\nTo learn more about Azure Linux, refer to our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n### What is Nginx?\n\nNginx (pronounced \"engine-x\") is an open-source reverse proxy server for HTTP, HTTPS, SMTP, POP3, and IMAP protocols, as well as a load balancer, HTTP cache, and a web server (origin server). The nginx project started with a strong focus on high concurrency, high performance, and low memory usage. It is licensed under the 2-clause BSD-like license and it runs on Linux, BSD variants, Mac OS X, Solaris, AIX, HP-UX, as well as on other *nix flavors. It also has a proof-of-concept port for Microsoft Windows.\nSee: [Nginx - Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nginx)\n\n## Featured tags\n\n- `1`\n\nThe featured tags are multi-architecture tags (i.e., `x86-64` and `aarch64`) that refer to the latest version of the image. Additional tags that are specific to nginx version, Azure Linux build, or architecture can be found in the Tags section.\n\n## Usage\n\n### Nginx configuration folder\n\nThe default location for the nginx configuration folder is: `/etc/nginx/`. The nginx's primary configuration file is `nginx.conf`. It has an include directive at the end of the file i.e., `include /etc/nginx/nginx.conf.default;`. If you'd like to provide your nginx default file, then consider naming it `/etc/nginx/nginx.conf.default`.\n\n### Hosting some simple static content\n\n`1.` Create a Dockerfile to generate a new image that includes the necessary content.\n\n    FROM mcr.microsoft.com/azurelinux/base/nginx:1\n    COPY static-html-directory /usr/share/nginx/html\n\n`2.` Place this file in the same directory as your directory of content (“static-html-directory”). Then build your container image.\n\n    docker build -t static-html-nginx .\n\n`3.` Start your container.\n\n    docker run -d -p 8080:80 static-html-nginx\n\nThe default container startup command is `\"nginx\", \"-g\", \"daemon off;\"`.\n\n### Launch Azure Linux shell\n\nThe nginx image ships with a bash shell. The launch command can be provided to docker run command to Launch Azure Linux shell. The following command will launch the shell:\n\n    docker run -it --rm mcr.microsoft.com/azurelinux/base/nginx:1 /bin/bash\n\n## Support\n\nAzure Linux container images are supported only for internal Microsoft use. For more information please see our [Support Statement](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/-/SUPPORT.md).\n\n## License\n\nThe Azure Linux distribution is provided under the [MIT license](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/-/LICENSE). Individual packages and components are governed by their own licenses included in the package sources available via srpm on [packages.microsoft.com](https://packages.microsoft.com/azurelinux/) or via our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n- Legal Notice: [Container License Information](https://aka.ms/mcr/osslegalnotice)","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"Microsoft","url":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/","official":true,"verified":true},"registered":null,"updated":"2026-09-12T02:11:20.6225866+00:00","categories":[],"keywords":[],"license":"MIT","links":[],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":null,"pullsText":"556K+","stars":null},"mediaTypes":[],"conte